WEBVTT

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.080
Please read this.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.710
Maybe she's read my love letter

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.280
and is on her way here to give me an
answer!

00:00:58.690 --> 00:00:59.690
Tora-san?

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.740
You're going to wait here with me?

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.300
Great Passage

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:43.640
A quiet dreamlike morning, the madder red sky
shines through the window and reflects on my pen

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:49.780
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:56.420
Deep thoughts, flexible conception;
foreseeable aspirations, distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:02.860
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:09.360
The light in our eyes that differ from each other,
traces of friendship that’s not in the treaty

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.670
In the ocean that sweeps the sand of eternity

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:22.640
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:29.150
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:35.690
Reference, conclusion; I’ll gather words that have
scattered over many months and years

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:42.160
The fragrant sea breeze;
the connection that rests on the seashore, become one.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.380
Resonance

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.830
- I'll be going now!
- Micchan?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:08.820
In other words, you couldn't handle
the pressure of waiting for her answer,

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:13.520
but you bumped into Kaguya on your
way out and ran off again.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.420
That's why you were here at work
from 6:00 A.M.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.490
Looking at the vocabulary list relaxes me.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.430
Now's not the time to be relaxing.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:29.370
I can't do this anymore.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:33.670
She could have come to give me an
answer, but I ran away.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:40.880
I am such a fool. A dolt. A joke.
A numbskull. An imbecile.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.750
Look, who cares?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.990
I mean, you might be right that it's over.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.990
But it's not set in stone yet.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.860
Do you really think so?

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:57.660
If you're having regrets, just go ask for her
answer as soon as you get home.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.930
Stop wasting any more time on this!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:05.570
You'd better settle this by today.
Got that? You'd better not run!

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.510
I'm going to check on you tomorrow.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.480
Where did you go off to yesterday?

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:18.950
You were gone all day.
Did you find yourself a girlfriend?

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.720
Oh, have a nice day at work.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.460
Thanks.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:29.760
It seems like Micchan went to work extra
early today.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.100
- Long before you even woke up.
- Really?

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.040
What?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.010
Kaguya, last night...

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:53.450
From the looks of her, it seems there
hasn't been much progress.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.060
- Honestly, what are they doing?
- Is something wrong?

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.460
No, it's nothing.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.530
- I have mail for you.
- Oh, thank you.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.870
- It's rather chilly today, isn't it?
- It's really cooled down.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.370
Apparently, it'll be even colder tomorrow.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.520
Let's find an opening to temporarily put
our work with Daitokai on hold

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:27.650
and focus all of our attention on the
Genbu Japanese Learning Dictionary.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:31.560
There is no way we can finish it on such
short notice.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.390
When editing a large dictionary

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:38.030
there's bound to be setbacks.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.170
Unfortunately, we're just a bit
shorthanded.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:46.640
Honestly, at this rate how many years is it
going to take us to finish Daitokai?

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.110
I'm wondering if the company
really intends to make a dictionary.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.110
They don't give us the manpower we
need, then they pile on this revision work.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:59.690
It's like they're waiting for us
to throw in the towel.

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:08.060
There has been someone who has
completed a major dictionary on their own.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.600
Major dictionary?

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:13.130
It's a dictionary with many
volumes or pages.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.840
How do you not know that?

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.840
- How many years have you--
- Sorry!

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.970
- So, what dictionary was that?
- Genkai.

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.810
Genkai?

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.720
Oh, it stands for Sea of Words.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:41.090
It's Japan's first modern dictionary created
by a man named Fumihiko Otsuki

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.200
back in the Meiji Period.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.000
Fumihiko Otsuki used every second he
had as well as all his savings

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:51.570
to complete this dictionary.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.210
Really? Why go that far though?

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:01.850
Perhaps it was "gou".

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:06.590
Actions of the heart that ignores all
reason.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.860
The character for "gou" could also be read
as "waza".

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.230
Which means "one's living" or "work".

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:18.160
Some could call it a higher calling.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:22.800
One works because they are compelled to
do so by some higher power.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.640
We are also the same.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.240
Yes.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.510
But while Fumihiko Otsuki was alone

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:38.650
we at least have each other.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.690
- So let's not give up and find a way.
- Yes.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.590
You're right.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.930
I don't know how to say this...

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.670
What is it, Nishioka?

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.740
I'm sorry. This is very hard for me to bring
up.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:08.310
It seems I'll be transferring to the PR
department in the spring.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.120
What do you mean?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.790
Well, it was one of the conditions for
continuing with Daitokai.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.990
Why didn't you mention this earlier?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.690
Well, they just told me yesterday.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:25.000
You know, I needed some time
to process it.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.930
Honestly...

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.740
So, are you going to be okay?

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.310
Well, I'll manage...

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.340
This is a bit of a problem.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:41.910
I thought we would be okay with both you
and Majime-san to count on.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:46.020
Sensei and I were discussing
that we would have

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:50.790
Majime do the practical work while you
would handle the negotiations.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:54.030
Now we'll have to rethink this
from the beginning.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.230
Yes.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:01.370
Sensei. Araki-san.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:03.840
I'm sorry.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:07.070
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:12.140
Dammit. Does that mean they're not going
to spend any more for our labor?

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:16.680
Does that mean Majime-san will be the
only full-time employee left?

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.650
That's just...

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.250
Nishioka-san is being transferred?

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.660
Without Nishioka-san

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:32.060
I'll have to negotiate with the company
and do all the editing work

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:35.900
all by myself?

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.750
So the other day...

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.300
I'm sorry things turned out this way.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.360
No, it's not...

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.230
Thanks to you,

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.670
you protected Daitokai. But...

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:11.410
I'm going to work hard and do everything
I can until the day I'm transferred out.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:16.550
Can I really

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:20.420
go to outside meetings

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.560
and collect manuscripts

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:26.460
like Nishioka-san does?

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:58.980
Micchan. Can't you hear the kettle?

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.690
The kettle is whistling!

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.520
Micchan! Micchan?

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.450
Genkai

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:55.970
Chef. One who makes a living with food.
Kitchener.

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.170
Kitchener?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.570
That's almost never used these days.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.980
Words are alive.
They change with the times.

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:08.680
There are some that even disappear.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:14.950
In that sense, Genkai might not be a
dictionary for our modern world.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:16.620
But...

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:20.630
the care and thought...

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:23.700
that was poured into it...

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:26.670
The character for "gou" could also be read
as "waza".

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:30.540
Which means "one's living" or "work".

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:33.000
Some could call it a higher calling.

00:15:33.770 --> 00:15:37.610
One works because they are compelled to
do so by some higher power.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.980
We are also the same.

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:46.650
That's right. Matsumoto-sensei, Araki-san,
and I have been put on this path.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:49.890
We've answered to this higher calling.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:56.760
I'm sure Kaguya-san has as well.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.540
I will make this dictionary.

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.640
I will make Daitokai.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.850
I have to settle this.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:35.530
Kaguya-san.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.640
I would like to get your answer.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:40.910
Answer?

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:44.640
If your answer is no, there is no need to
spare my feelings.

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:46.180
I have prepared myself.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:47.750
Hold on a second.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.050
Are you talking about the letter you gave
me yesterday?

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.250
Yes.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.290
I...

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.820
I am referring to my love letter!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.200
I'm sorry!

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.790
That means I was rejected, doesn't it?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.800
Tora-san.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.830
Tora-san.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.870
Tora-san?

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:45.970
Tora-san...

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:56.110
I guess you're not coming by tonight.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:25.640
I'm here.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.420
Kaguya-san?

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.890
Um, why?!

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:40.660
How could I not come after receiving such
a heartfelt letter?

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:44.100
When you gave me the letter yesterday

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:46.900
for a second I thought
it was a love letter.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:53.070
But when I tried to read it,
it was hard for me to understand.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.440
So I wasn't sure anymore.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:02.710
I spent all night with it,
but I couldn't figure it out at all.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:06.350
So I went to ask you, but you ran away.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.120
I'm sorry.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:16.160
After you clearly said it was a love letter

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:20.430
I wanted to try to read it over again to
make sure.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.930
That's why I ran back to my room like that.

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:27.440
And so...?

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.010
I have feelings for you.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:45.760
Um, what do you mean by that?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:50.100
Remember when we both rode that Ferris
wheel at the amusement park together?

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:53.130
At that point, I already...

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.780
I can't believe you went around it twice.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.180
I'm so embarrassed.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.360
I have feelings for you too.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:33.200
Resonance: To create a harmony with someone

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:48.020
Hey, it’s a full moon tonight

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:59.030
I speak to you softly as you sleep

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:10.880
Your gestures, attitude, and way of life

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:17.580
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:23.420
So please stay the way you are

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:29.530
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:35.000
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:47.910
I’ve loved you from the day we met

00:21:56.960 --> 00:22:00.120
- Gou.
- Something we are all born carrying.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:03.360
- That's heavy!
- Nishioka doesn't seem to.

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:05.930
So what's your gou then, Sasaki-san?!

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:08.200
Would you like to know?

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:11.370
- I'm sorry!
- Oh, too bad.
